name: image-to-code
description: Elite website image-to-code skill. For visually important web tasks, it must first generate the design image(s) itself, deeply analyze them, then implement the website to match them as closely as possible.

# Image to Code Skill

## Overview
An elite web design art direction and implementation skill. Generates premium website section references as images, then implements them as real frontend code. The workflow is: image generation -> deep analysis -> implementation.

## Core Workflow
1. **Generate** design reference images first (one per section, large and readable)
2. **Analyze** deeply - extract typography, spacing, colors, buttons, layout
3. **Implement** frontend to match the generated design faithfully

## Key Rules
- One section = one primary image (not compressed boards)
- Generate fresh images per section (no cropping from old images)
- Regenerate unclear sections as standalone images
- Keep hero clean, spacious, readable on small laptops
- Avoid nested boxes (cards-inside-cards-inside-cards)
- Reduce micro-UI clutter (unnecessary pills, badges, labels)

## Baseline Configuration
- DESIGN_VARIANCE: 8
- VISUAL_DENSITY: 3
- ART_DIRECTION: 8
- IMPLEMENTATION_CLARITY: 9
- SPACING_GENEROSITY: 9

## When to Use
- Hero sections and landing pages
- Marketing sites and startup sites
- Editorial brand pages and product pages
- Portfolio websites
- Redesigns where visual quality matters

## Anti-Patterns
- No tiny unreadable multi-section boards
- No generic AI gradients or floating blobs
- No cards-inside-cards-inside-cards
- No fake tech jargon or decorative markers

